  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1135 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nWeak cold front is expected to move into NE OK Sunday morning and\nmove slowly southward through the day. The exact location varies\namongst guidance but along and north of the boundary expect\nisolated to scattered afternoon thunderstorms to develop. Large\nt/td spreads and deep inverted V profiles favor potential for strong\ndownbursts through Sunday evening. Additional storms developing\nacross the High Plains may spread eastward Sunday night into\nMonday while weakening. Higher rain chances will favor areas north\nof Interstate 40 with any meaningful rainfall amounts expected to\nremain spotty.\n\nTemperatures and heat index values may spike again on Sunday with\nhot pre frontal temps and pooled moisture along and north of the\nboundary providing no appreciable heat stress relief. A similar\nnorth to south gradient in temperatures is likely on Monday,\nhowever overall heat index relief will be minimal. \n\nThe boundary loses definition as upper ridging intensifies by\nTuesday with very hot temperatures returning area wide Tuesday and\nWednesday. Upper ridge may build westward by late week and allow a\nmore substantial trough and associated cold frontal passage by\nlate next week. Uncertainties increase at this time range but a\nglimmer of hope from the hot and dry weather.",
